{
  "slug": "op-ed-writing",
  "concept": "Op-ed writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "The op-ed is the shortest serious argument form in public writing. In ~750 words you must make a single argument that a previously-uninterested reader believes by the end. Every deviation from convent",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The op-ed is the shortest serious argument form in public writing. In ~750 words you must make a single argument that a previously-uninterested reader believes by the end. Every deviation from convention is a friction point that costs pickup.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "One argument. A piece that tries to make two arguments makes neither.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. Word count and the 750-word discipline",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Standard target: 750 words. New York Times caps at 800. Washington Post caps at 800. Most regional dailies sit at 600–700.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#1-word-count-and-the-750-word-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. The single thesis",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The thesis is one sentence. It is a claim someone could disagree with.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#2-the-single-thesis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Tests for a strong op-ed thesis:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#2-the-single-thesis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Disagreeable. \"Schools should teach reading\" is not a thesis.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#2-the-single-thesis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Singular. \"We need to fix housing, healthcare, and education\" is three theses.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#2-the-single-thesis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Provable in 750 words.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#2-the-single-thesis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Front-loaded. The thesis appears in the first paragraph.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#2-the-single-thesis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. \"Why now\" — the news peg",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Op-eds are not evergreen. Every published op-ed has a reason it ran this week. Acceptable pegs:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#3-why-now-the-news-peg",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "A news event - a bill introduced, a court ruling, an election result",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#3-why-now-the-news-peg",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "A counter to recent coverage",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#3-why-now-the-news-peg",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "The op-ed \"why now\" is why this argument matters this week, not \"why I'm releasing this product this week.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#3-why-now-the-news-peg",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. The authority paragraph — \"why I'm qualified to say this\"",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Forms of authority editors accept:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#4-the-authority-paragraph-why-im-qualified-to-say-this",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Direct professional experience. \"I spent fifteen years as an immigration attorney.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#4-the-authority-paragraph-why-im-qualified-to-say-this",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Subject of the issue. \"I am one of the 8 million Americans whose student loans are in default.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#4-the-authority-paragraph-why-im-qualified-to-say-this",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Reporting access. \"I have spent the last six months interviewing the engineers who designed the system.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#4-the-authority-paragraph-why-im-qualified-to-say-this",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Forms of authority that fail:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#4-the-authority-paragraph-why-im-qualified-to-say-this",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Generic credentials. \"I am a thought leader in this space.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#4-the-authority-paragraph-why-im-qualified-to-say-this",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Title without specifics. \"As a CEO, I want to say...\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#4-the-authority-paragraph-why-im-qualified-to-say-this",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Structure: the 8-paragraph skeleton",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Hook + thesis (80–120 words). One concrete image, anecdote, or fact; the thesis in the last sentence.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#5-structure-the-8-paragraph-skeleton",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Why now (60–100 words). The news peg.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#5-structure-the-8-paragraph-skeleton",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Authority (40–80 words). Why the reader should listen to you.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#5-structure-the-8-paragraph-skeleton",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence beat 1 (80–120 words). The first reason the thesis is correct.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#5-structure-the-8-paragraph-skeleton",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence beat 2 (80–120 words). The second reason.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#5-structure-the-8-paragraph-skeleton",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Counter-argument and rebuttal (100–150 words). The strongest objection, named and answered.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#5-structure-the-8-paragraph-skeleton",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Stakes / consequence (60–100 words). What happens if we ignore this.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#5-structure-the-8-paragraph-skeleton",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Call to action / kicker (50–100 words). The specific thing the reader should do.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#5-structure-the-8-paragraph-skeleton",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Counter-argument acknowledgment",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The piece must name the strongest objection to your thesis and answer it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#6-counter-argument-acknowledgment",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Strawman counter. Picking a weak version of the opposing view.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#6-counter-argument-acknowledgment",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Both-sides-ism. Treating the counter so generously you've made the opposing case better than your own.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#6-counter-argument-acknowledgment",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Evidence selection",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Evidence in an op-ed is brutally selective. You have room for 2–4 evidence claims at most. Each one must be:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#7-evidence-selection",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Concrete. A number, a named case, a specific policy.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#7-evidence-selection",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Recent. Data from the last 1–3 years.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#7-evidence-selection",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Citable. Every factual claim must be checkable.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#7-evidence-selection",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Voice and register",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Op-eds are written in first person, conversational-but-controlled prose. No jargon. No hedging escalators. No headers. No bullet lists.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#8-voice-and-register",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. The call-to-action close",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every op-ed ends with a specific actionable claim:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#9-the-call-to-action-close",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "A policy that should pass or fail.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#9-the-call-to-action-close",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "A practice an industry should adopt or abandon.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#9-the-call-to-action-close",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "An institution that should change a specific procedure.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#9-the-call-to-action-close",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "10. Pitch and submission mechanics",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Submit the full piece, not a pitch.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#10-pitch-and-submission-mechanics",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Subject line. \"Op-ed submission: [4-7 word headline].\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#10-pitch-and-submission-mechanics",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Bio. 25–40 words at the bottom.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#10-pitch-and-submission-mechanics",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Expect silence. Standard expectation is no response within 3 business days = pass.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#10-pitch-and-submission-mechanics",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Worked thesis-to-skeleton example",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Topic: Database security audits at small companies.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#worked-thesis-to-skeleton-example",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Thesis: \"Small SaaS companies should be required by their cyber-insurance carriers to run quarterly database audits.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#worked-thesis-to-skeleton-example",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Why now: Recent breach at [named company] traced to an un-audited database.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#worked-thesis-to-skeleton-example",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence beats: (1) Audit findings data - % of un-audited dbs with critical flaws. (2) Cost comparison - quarterly audit vs. one breach.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#worked-thesis-to-skeleton-example",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Counter: \"This is regulatory overreach.\" Answer: Insurance is private; carriers already underwrite for fire suppression.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#worked-thesis-to-skeleton-example",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "CTA: Insurance industry should adopt the standard at the June meeting.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#worked-thesis-to-skeleton-example",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The \"we need a conversation\" piece. Ends with a call for dialogue instead of an actionable claim.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The five-thesis piece. Tries to argue about five things in 800 words.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The disguised press release. \"Our company has been working on this issue for years...\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The strawman counter.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The evergreen piece. No news peg.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The 1,400-word \"short\" version. If you can't get it to 800, you don't have one argument.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/op-ed-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
